# Adding / pulling an MF remote (polyrepo)

Platform git = **shell + packages + tools**. Remotes are **separate git repos**,
optionally checked out under `apps/<name>` (gitignored by platform).

Do **not** hand-copy vite configs, shell remotes, router routes, or sider links.

## Pull an existing remote (most common)

```bash
bun run pull-remote --name promotions
bun run pull-remote --all
bun run pull-remote --name orders --force   # replace local checkout
```

Needs `"repo"` on the remote in `packages/mf-config/remotes.json`
(git URL or `template:<folder>` under `templates/`).

## Scaffold a new remote

```bash
nx g @react-mfe/workspace-plugin:remote orders --port=5104 --no-interactive
# optional: --title=Orders --blurb="…" --repo=https://git…/orders.git --prodEntry=https://…/remoteEntry.js
```

Or: `bun run create-remote --name=orders --port=5104`

Then init/push `apps/<name>` as its **own** git repo and set `"repo"` in remotes.json.

## What updates

| Piece | Where | Manual? |
| ----- | ----- | ------- |
| Registry | `packages/mf-config/remotes.json` | generator / you |
| Local app | `apps/<name>/` | generator or pull-remote |
| Shell MF / routes / sider | read `REMOTES` | auto |
| `bun run dev` | only **checked-out** remotes + shell | auto |

## Local checkout only

```bash
bun run drop-remote --name promotions   # delete apps/promotions, keep registry
```

## Unregister entirely

```bash
bun run delete-remote --name promotions
```

Stop `bun run dev` first on Windows (`EACCES` / `EBUSY`).
